{"id": "1bf99ecc-35e9-4125-8a41-4ba78b2d4da5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit both. I'm checking SageMaker notebook instances and Studio domains separately across the associated accounts and regions, looking at internet exposure and encryption at rest. This takes a few minutes.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_NdJdz7Bw9O4Gv0ouPsHGeH", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-notebook-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security audit of Amazon SageMaker NOTEBOOK INSTANCES for (a) internet exposure and (b) encryption at rest.",
  "context": "Customer wants a posture audit. Use list_associations to find all associated AWS accounts, and check every enabled region where SageMaker notebook instances exist (start with us-east-1 and any region where list_notebook_instances returns results; sweep commonly used regions). Agent space account is 012345678901_1. Use only read-only calls (list_/describe_). Do NOT modify anything.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker list_notebook_instances", "sagemaker describe_notebook_instance", "ec2 describe_security_groups / describe_subnets / describe_route_tables (for the notebook's subnet and SGs)", "kms describe_key (for key type)"],
  "criteria": "For each notebook instance report: name, account, region, status; DirectInternetAccess (Enabled = exposed path to internet), SubnetId (none = SageMaker-managed internet-facing VPC), SecurityGroups and whether any allow 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 ingress, whether the subnet routes to an IGW/NAT, RootAccess, public URL accessibility via IAM; VolumeSizeInGB and KmsKeyId (missing = no customer-managed KMS key on the ML storage volume; note whether AWS-managed vs customer-managed key if set); also note IMDSv1 vs v2 (InstanceMetadataServiceConfiguration). Give a severity rating (High/Medium/Low) per finding and a concise remediation. Return a compact table plus a short summary with counts. If there are no notebook instances in an account/region, say so briefly."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebook instances for exposure and encryption"}, {"id": "tooluse_CwywnLJOWZjxE9SxhpErlS", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-domain-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security audit of Amazon SageMaker (Studio) DOMAINS for (a) internet exposure and (b) encryption at rest.",
  "context": "Customer wants a posture audit. Use list_associations to find all associated AWS accounts, and check every enabled region where SageMaker domains exist (start with us-east-1; sweep commonly used regions). Agent space account is 012345678901_1. Use only read-only calls (list_/describe_). Do NOT modify anything.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker list_domains", "sagemaker describe_domain", "sagemaker list_user_profiles / list_spaces (spot check)", "ec2 describe_security_groups / describe_subnets / describe_route_tables / describe_vpc_endpoints for the domain VPC", "kms describe_key"],
  "criteria": "For each domain report: domain id/name, account, region, status, AuthMode, AppNetworkAccessType (PublicInternetOnly = exposed internet path; VpcOnly = no direct internet), VPC/subnets/security groups and whether SGs allow 0.0.0.0/0 ingress or the subnets route to an IGW, presence of VPC endpoints (sagemaker.api, sagemaker.runtime, studio, s3) for VpcOnly domains, KmsKeyId for the EFS home directory volume (missing = AWS-managed/service-managed key rather than customer-managed), ProductionKmsKeyId / default space settings, and any user profile or space-level overrides to public networking where easy to see. Give a severity rating (High/Medium/Low) per finding and a concise remediation. Return a compact table plus a short summary with counts. If there are no domains in an account/region, say so briefly."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker Studio domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

